codex
The final audit exposed a substantive benchmark-quality issue before handoff: the renderer was explicitly printing the planted rank-one direction and the one-coordinate perturbations. That made the compact route too close to being handed over, even though the local attacks passed. I’m tightening the presentation so the solver receives only the paper-native dense quadratic matrix and full label vectors; the hidden direction must actually be recognized. I’m also moving to 14 phases at dimension 83, which keeps the compact route under 300 operations while preserving stronger structure-aware guess resistance.
