wc -l llm_loop_transcript.jsonl g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl" in /home/gson/gvrepo/results/2605.17594
 succeeded in 0ms:
     1	# Exact MUB overlap phases from rank-one bent quadratics
     2	
     3	| profile | value |
     4	|---|---|
     5	| track | **B — no-tool compression** |
     6	| native domain | algebra |
     7	| object regime | finite field |
     8	| computational core | linear algebra |
     9	| certificate form | exact symbolic |
    10	| intended intuition | symmetry: detect a scalar identity plus a rank-one form |
    11	| domain essentiality | native |
    12	| reduction | none |
    13	
    14	This generator is based on William M. Kantor’s [“MUBs from bent
    15	functions”](https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.17594). It hands the solver a symmetric
    16	quadratic-form matrix `Q` over `F_3` and fourteen linear label differences.
    17	For every one of fourteen labels it asks for the exact additive-character sum that is the inner
    18	product of two of the paper’s unnormalised MUB phase vectors. The answer is a
    19	compact factorisation in the exact ring
    20	`Z[zeta]/(zeta^2+zeta+1)`, not a floating-point approximation.
    21	
    22	Trust status: all local G1–G9(c) gates pass. The mandatory four-vendor oracle
    23	claim is **not complete**: all bare, structural-hint, and placebo requests
    24	returned HTTP 403 `Key limit exceeded (total limit)` before any model produced
    25	an answer. The transcript files are the harness’s genuine error records, but
    26	errors are not counted as failures. This directory is therefore not ready for
    27	submission until those three script-owned runs are repeated with OpenRouter
    28	quota.
    29	
    30	## Construction and Track B claim
    31	
    32	Section 2 defines
    33	`e_(a,B)=sum_v zeta^(a·v+B(v)) e_v`, defines bent differences, and proves in
    34	Theorem 2.1 that a mubent set produces mutually unbiased bases. Example 2.2
    35	specialises to quadratic functions `v M v^T/2`: nonsingular matrix differences
    36	are bent. Section 4 explains that the construction is not a new classification
    37	and that essentially all known odd-characteristic examples are quadratic.
    38	
    39	For each generated instance,
    40	
    41	```text
    42	Q = lambda I + mu r r^T  over F_3,
    43	det(Q) = lambda^(n-1) (lambda + mu r^T r),
    44	Q^-1 = lambda^-1 I
    45	       - mu lambda^-1 (lambda + mu r^T r)^-1 r r^T.
    46	```
    47	
    48	The generator samples these factors first and composes the determinant and
    49	inverse identities to obtain its witness. It never runs the dense solver.
    50	Completing the square gives the exact overlap
    51	
    52	```text
    53	alpha_j = chi(det Q) (-1-2*zeta)^n zeta^(d_j^T Q^-1 d_j).
    54	```
    55	
    56	The checker independently performs dense Gauss–Jordan elimination over `F_3`,
    57	recomputes the determinant character and every quadratic phase, and compares
    58	them exactly. This is an efficient `O(n^3+q n^2)` algorithm, so the family makes
    59	no Track A claim. At shipping size it used 746,470 field operations in the
    60	fixed G5 measurement and averaged 747,532 operations over eight G6 seeds
    61	(0.018 s and 0.018 s on this host). The compact rank-one route uses at most 297
    62	field operations. The paper makes magnitudes immediate, so asking only for
    63	`|alpha|^2` would be an easy constant-answer family; fourteen varying exact
    64	phases avoid that regime.
    65	
    66	## Worked demo
    67	
    68	`make_instance(n=3, queries=3, changes=1, seed=0)` renders the following full
    69	instance:
    70	
    71	```text
    72	Exact phases of quadratic MUB overlaps over F_3
    73	
    74	All arithmetic in exponents is modulo 3.  Let F_3={0,1,2} and let zeta be
    75	a formal primitive cube root of unity, so zeta^3=1 and
    76	zeta^2+zeta+1=0.  Vectors have 3 coordinates indexed 0 through 2.
    77	
    78	For the symmetric 3 by 3 matrix Q below and each listed label vector d_j,
    79	define the exact character sum
    80	
    81	  alpha_j = sum over x in F_3^3 of
    82	            zeta^( 2*x^T*Q*x + d_j^T*x ).
    83	
    84	Here 2 is 1/2 in F_3.  These are inner products of the unnormalised phase
    85	vectors e_(a,B) used for mutually unbiased bases: Q is the matrix of the
    86	quadratic bent-function difference and d_j is the label difference.  The
    87	given Q is nonsingular, but no factorisation or inverse is supplied.
    88	
    89	Q (one space-separated row per line):
    90	1 2 1
    91	2 1 1
    92	1 1 1
    93	END_Q
    94	
    95	Label vectors d_j (query index, then 3 space-separated residues):
    96	0 1 2 2
    97	1 1 0 0
    98	2 1 1 1
    99	END_LABELS
   100	
   101	Return one exact factorised certificate.  The integer sign must be -1 or 1,
   102	and phases must contain exactly 3 integers, in query order, each in
   103	{0,1,2}, such that for every j
   104	
   105	  alpha_j = sign * (-1 - 2*zeta)^3 * zeta^phases[j].
   106	
   107	The equality is exact in Z[zeta]/(zeta^2+zeta+1); no decimal approximation is
   108	allowed.  Query order matters and repetitions among phase values are allowed.
   109	
   110	Give your final answer inside <answer></answer> tags as one JSON object with
   111	keys "sign" and "phases".  Format-only example:
   112	<answer>{"sign":1,"phases":[0,0,0]}</answer>
   113	Output nothing else inside the tags.
   114	```
   115	
   116	Its answer is `<answer>{"sign":-1,"phases":[1,0,1]}</answer>`.
   117	`verify(inst, inst["answer"])` returns `(True, "ok")`; dropping the last phase
   118	returns `(False, "too few phases: expected 3, got 2")`. The demo is genuinely
   119	hand-scale: it has only 27 summands per overlap, although the rank-one route is
   120	shorter.
   121	
   122	## Difficulty presets
   123	
   124	| preset | dimension | queries | rendered chars (seed 0) | answer atoms | status |
   125	|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|
   126	| demo | 3 | 3 | 1,477 | 4 | hand example; skipped by hardening |
   127	| easy | 23 | 14 | 3,199 | 15 | local gates pass; oracle unavailable |
   128	| medium | 47 | 14 | 7,231 | 15 | local gates pass; oracle unavailable |
   129	| hard | 83 | 14 | 17,599 | 15 | **shipping candidate**; oracle unavailable |
   130	
   131	`escalate()` raises only the ambient matrix dimension, leaving the certificate
   132	at fifteen atoms. G7 verifies a dimension-166 instance, where the same answer
   133	shape replaces 5,279,816 dense field operations.
   134	
   135	## Gate results
   136	
   137	| gate | measured result |
   138	|---|---|
   139	| G1 | 12/12 planted witnesses and JSON round-trips; direct demo sums agree |
   140	| G2 | 5/5 corruptions rejected with five distinct reasons |
   141	| G3 | 3/3 tagged prose/fenced answers round-trip; garbage returns `None` |
   142	| G4 | 0/200,000 structure-aware guesses; exact probability `1/4,782,969` |
   143	| G5 | unique exact answer; 0/200,000 sampled; 746,470 operations, 0.018 s |
   144	| G6 | five attacks all 0/8; dense reference solves 8/8 as Track B expects |
   145	| G7 | dimension 166 verifies; 5,279,816 reference operations; answer still 15 atoms |
   146	| G8 | 20/20 GL+query-order invariance, 20/20 carried witnesses, 20/20 distinct keys |
   147	| G9(c) | 50 worst-case characters, 13 conservative tokens, 15 atoms, 297 intended operations |
   148	
   149	The machine-readable details are in
   150	[`selftest_report.json`](selftest_report.json).
   151	
   152	## Oracle loop and G9 arms
   153	
   154	| arm | completed attempts | solved | result |
   155	|---|---:|---:|---|
   156	| bare | 0 | 0 | four HTTP 403 total-limit errors; no hardness verdict |
   157	| structural hint | 0 | 0 | four HTTP 403 total-limit errors; diagnostic incomplete |
   158	| placebo hint | 0 | 0 | four HTTP 403 total-limit errors; diagnostic incomplete |
   159	
   160	Because no arm has a completed attempt, `hinted − placebo` is recorded as
   161	`0.0` only as a placeholder and supports no conclusion about the symmetry
   162	hint. The bare errors are preserved in
   163	[`llm_loop_transcript.jsonl`](llm_loop_transcript.jsonl); the two G9 error runs
   164	are preserved in [`g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl`](g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl) and
   165	[`g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl`](g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl).
   166	
   167	## Use
   168	
   169	```python
   170	from gen_2605_17594 import (DIFFICULTY, SHIPPING_DIFFICULTY,
   171	                            make_instance, parse_answer, render, verify)
   172	
   173	params = DIFFICULTY[SHIPPING_DIFFICULTY]
   174	inst = make_instance(seed=12345, **params)
   175	question = render(inst)
   176	candidate = parse_answer(model_output)
   177	ok, reason = verify(inst, candidate)
   178	```
   179	
   180	After rerunning and completing all three oracle arms, emit from the repository
   181	root with:
   182	
   183	```bash
   184	bash scripts/emit.sh 2605.17594 20 hard
   185	```
   186	
   187	## Caveats
   188	
   189	- The result is locally verified but not submission-ready until OpenRouter
   190	  quota permits the mandatory four-vendor runs. An API error is not evidence
   191	  that a model failed the problem.
   192	- `0/200,000` is a sample. The stronger exact number comes from the declared
   193	  structure-aware language: a random candidate is granted the correct
   194	  determinant sign and chooses fourteen independent ternary phases. It does not model a solver that has
   195	  partially recovered several phases.
   196	- Dense elimination takes only milliseconds with Python on this host. That is
   197	  expected and is why this is Track B; the claim is solely about recognizing
   198	  and executing the compact algebra without tools.
   199	- The attacks cover constant phases, label-weight outliers, a first-coordinate
   200	  greedy rule, a diagonal-only ansatz, and 256 random phase restarts. They do
   201	  not cover every possible symbolic-algebra heuristic or a model equipped with
   202	  a CAS.
   203	- The canonical key is invariant under arbitrary invertible coordinate changes
   204	  and query permutations and was collision-free on twenty unrelated seeds. Its
   205	  color-refined Gram invariant is not a complete canonizer for every possible
   206	  finite-field Gram graph.
   207	- The hard prompt is about 17.6k characters. Some oracle difficulty could come
   208	  from navigating the matrix as well as recognizing rank one. Once the hidden
   209	  all-nonzero direction is recognized, its norm is `n mod 3` and every full
   210	  label has one exceptional coordinate, keeping intended arithmetic below the
   211	  no-tool cap.
