Implemented and verified a native Track B generator based on Theorem 2.1 and Example 2.2 of [MUBs from bent functions](https://arxiv.org/html/2605.17594v1).

- [Generator](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2605.17594/gen_2605_17594.py)
- [Self-test report](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2605.17594/selftest_report.json)
- [README](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2605.17594/README.md)
- [Bare oracle transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2605.17594/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [Hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2605.17594/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [Placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2605.17594/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

Results:

- All G1–G9 gates pass.
- Shipping preset: `medium`, with `n=47` and 14 overlap queries.
- Dense reference algorithm: 160,211 field operations.
- Compact rank-one route: at most 261 operations.
- Guess probability: `1 / 4,782,969`; sampled hits `0/200,000`.
- Bare hardening: `easy` was solved, then `medium` held `0/3`.
- G9: bare `0/3`, hinted `1/3`, placebo `1/3`; structural lift `0.0`.
- Caveat: the current harness used two vendors, and two shipping failures were empty provider content-filter responses. This is documented prominently in the README.
